Package: ladybird-app
Name: Ladybird
Version: @VER@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libicu78 (>= 78.3), libiosexec1 (>= 1.3.1)
Section: Apps
Priority: optional
MinimumOSVersion: 16.0
Description: Ladybird — a standalone native web browser for jailbroken iOS
 A real home-screen browser app: tap the icon, it launches standalone (no iosc /
 Wayland / desktop stack) and renders the modern web with the from-scratch Ladybird
 engine (LibWeb + LibJS, no WebKit, no JIT).
 .
 Built and validated on iPad. The bundle also declares iPhone (UIDeviceFamily 1) and
 the frontend is resolution- and safe-area-independent, but no iPhone has been tested.
 .
 This M0 package bundles the Ladybird UI executable, helper processes, runtime dylib
 closure, resources, and fonts inside Ladybird.app. The helpers are spawned from the app
 bundle and use Ladybird's Mach bootstrap IPC on iOS.
 .
 Painting requires IOSurface-backed front buffers presented through Metal, and the
 release Compositor links real ANGLE/EGL/GLES. The build fails closed instead of
 silently shipping a software or trap-stub rendering path.
